{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1490954-psions-and-superiors-in-aberrant","id":1490954,"title":"Psions and Superiors in Aberrant.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-21T17:07:13-07:00","id":1490954,"title":"Psions and Superiors in Aberrant.","content":"A thought for a AU (sadly, I think AU's are still banned for the storyvault, so here it is)--what if the Psions and Superiors were created some time before the Aberrant War. We know that things were getting bad before everything kicked off, so you could either have:<br /> 1. A mega intelligent nova working with some psiad helpers figuring out how to create a prometheus chamber of his own. <br /> 2. A faction of the Doyen being uncharacteristically fast moving and providing them as a hope of controlling the aberrant. <br /> <br /> Regardless, you start to get full-fledged. psions, perhaps working for Aeon, perhaps working for a government, along with superiors, appearing oh, say, ten years before the Aberrant war Could psions and superiors be able to keep things from falling apart to the degree they did? Could they prevent the Chinese Ultimatum and the war?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T17:33:02-07:00","id":1490956,"title":"","content":"There is one Tasty Bit coming soon with Psion in modern Age.<br /> <br /> I won\u2019t believe the Psions would change the balance unless you have a amazing number of them around. Novas are too powerful and too few, if you add a reasonable number of Psions capable of balancing things up, you may have enough to prevent Aberrant war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T23:40:57-08:00","id":1504335,"title":"","content":"I forget the proper term for the non-alien-magic-bathtub psions, but they <i>are</i> canon in both editions. Some of them predate the Aberrant War by decades and the Aeons were apparently both aware of the possibility and overtly seeking them out, as I read things.<br /> <br /> You'd need enough power represented by such a group to make a big difference, but, frankly, there's an argument to be made that the survival of humanity as something other than a nearly extinct slave race or pets in the <b>official</b> timeline argues that great progress was made to curtail the problems posed by the Aberrants.<br /> <br /> I don't see any reason why you couldn't have some better outcomes. You could have the good novas beat out the naughtyspawn. (which includes both novas &amp; AEon)<br /> <br /> Heck, you could decide that one of the more powerful nova was so incredibly torqued off at the offences against him and his that he diverged the timeline and made sure what he wanted went the way he preferred. Enjoy the possibility of Warp and Teleport having some really strange potential side effects like slipping into the alternate timeline where the clandestine sterilization of and experimentation on novas was forcefully curtailed and more rational legal protections both ways were put in place. A version of the Terragen, for instance, might exist with better self policing and actually be a powerful force for good. A balanced approach to Chrysalis and Dormancy might become a well-known and generally encouraged approach to the taint. (transcendance... whatever.) Flesh out the new problems imposed on that world.<br /> <br /> Players would also need to work out how to go home, if they wanted to.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-04T01:58:41-08:00","id":1504340,"title":"","content":"Well, I don\u2019t think adding more powered people and call them a different name is something that work without a strong \u201cus versus them\u201d and telepathic powers used in global scale.<br /> <br /> Psiads were present in the Nova era, and they were called Novas by everyone, including them selves. Aeon as an organization is not aware of the differences between psi and quantum (not even putting Flux in the middle), even with a number of their directors aware of that. Think the armed forces/CIA/FBI and all the secret projects, do you think a random riffle-man/agent knows about it?<br /> <br /> Another point is, Novas fought in the humanity side, I would even say more novas were on the humanity side than in the Aberrant side. The number of Novas is so small and their powers can be so intense, there is no effective war against them. It\u2019s guerrilla tactics, what is usually hard to deal with common armed forces, but with people capable of leveling cities (or states) by mistake. You can have a quantum detector in satellites, and weapons of mass destruction pointed to them, but if you use you kill far more normal people than Aberrants (and some of them would not die for a simple nuclear strike). Just think that Superman x Zod fight in Man of Steel and all the destruction caused while their were fighting watch other (not aiming the general population) or the fight of Invincible versus Omniman (the guy was holding back to not kill the boy).<br /> <br /> Another point is the war is not caused by pure Taint/Transcendence, there is a much more human aspect of it all, prejudice. Imagine you are capable of doing all that things and random people start treating you bad, or trying to block your way to visit your family, or try to make you lose your job. Now think about what people do under stress, don\u2019t need to be crazy people, they try to hit policemen, try to run away in their cars, some even shoot people hoping it nobody will see. Now add scale to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}